             attention layers. Used by models with hybrid local/global attention (e.g., Gemma 3)
             which use different RoPE bases for local (10k) and global (1M) attention. Defaults
             to None, which means the standard rotary_base is used for all layers.
+        d_head_local (int, *optional*): Head dimension for local-attention layers, when it
+            differs from the global-attention head dimension (`d_head`). Gemma 4 is the
+            motivating case: sliding/local layers use head_dim=256 while full/global layers
+            use head_dim=512. Defaults to None, meaning `d_head` applies to every layer
+            (every model except Gemma 4 as of this addition).
+        n_key_value_heads_local (int, *optional*): Number of KV-head groups for
+            local-attention layers, when it differs from `n_key_value_heads` (Gemma 4:
+            16 for sliding/local layers vs. 4 for full/global layers). Defaults to None,
+            meaning `n_key_value_heads` applies to every layer.
+        rotary_dim_local (int, *optional*): Rotary dimension for local-attention layers, when
+            it differs from the global-attention `rotary_dim` (Gemma 4: full rotary over
+            d_head_local=256 on local layers vs. a 0.25 partial-rotary-factor over
+            d_head=512, i.e. rotary_dim=128, on global layers). Defaults to None, meaning
+            `rotary_dim` applies to every layer.
+        use_v_norm (bool): Whether to apply an unscaled RMSNorm to the value projection
+            before attention (Gemma 4: every layer's value path is RMS-normalized with no
+            learned scale, mirroring q_norm/k_norm's mechanism but without a weight -- see
+            `use_qk_norm`). Defaults to False.
         norm_topk_prob (bool): Whether to normalize the top-k probabilities in the MoE layer.
         use_logn_attn (bool): Qwen-1's log-n attention: scale queries by
             log_{train_len}(position) past the training length (eval only).
@@ -297,6 +315,14 @@ class HookedTransformerConfig(TransformerLensConfig):
